## 2. Functional Requirements

### 2.1 Event Registration & Capacity

- Attendee can browse/search events by name, date, category
- Attendee can register for an event if seats remain
- System blocks registration automatically once an event reaches capacity
- Seats remaining is shown in real time on the event listing

### 2.2 Payment & Refund (mock)

- Paid events require a simulated checkout step before registration is confirmed
- A Payment record is created with status Pending, then updated to Completed (mock gateway, no real transaction)
- Free events (price = 0) skip the payment step entirely
- On cancellation, a refund is automatically triggered: Payment status changes to Refunded
- Attendee can view their payment/refund history
- Organizer/Admin can view all transactions for an event

### 2.3 Cancellation

- Attendee can cancel a confirmed registration before the event date
- Cancelling a paid registration triggers the refund flow (2.2)
- Cancelling frees up one seat on the event
- If a waitlist exists for that event, the next waitlisted attendee is automatically promoted (see 2.4)

### 2.4 Auto-Queuing (Waitlist)

- If an event is full, an attendee can join a waitlist instead of being blocked outright
- Waitlist is ordered first-in-first-out
- When a seat frees up (via cancellation), the system automatically promotes the next attendee on the waitlist to a confirmed registration
- Promoted attendee is notified (in-app) and, if the event is paid, goes through the payment step to confirm

### 2.5 QR Code Entry / Check-in

- On successful registration (and payment, if applicable), the system generates a unique QR code tied to that registration
- Attendee can view/download their QR ticket from 'My Registrations'
- Organizer uses a check-in screen to scan/enter the QR code and mark attendance
- Each QR code can only be used once — a second scan is flagged as 'already checked in'
- Organizer dashboard shows checked-in count vs. total registered

### 2.6 Dashboards

- **Attendee:** my upcoming events, my registrations, my payment history
- **Organizer:** event list, attendees per event, revenue per event, check-in status
- **Admin:** platform-wide overview of events and organizers

