## 4. User Stories & Acceptance Criteria

| Feature | User Story | Acceptance Criteria |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Registration | As an attendee, I want to register for an event so that I can attend it. | Registration blocked if seats = 0; seat count decreases by 1 on success. |
| Payment | As an attendee, I want to pay for a paid event so that my registration is confirmed. | Payment record created; status moves Pending → Completed; registration confirmed only after payment success. |
| Refund | As an attendee, I want a refund when I cancel a paid registration so that I get my money back. | Payment status changes to Refunded; refund amount matches original payment. |
| Cancellation | As an attendee, I want to cancel my registration so that I free up my seat. | Registration status = Cancelled; seat count increases by 1; refund triggered if paid. |
| Waitlist | As an attendee, I want to join a waitlist when an event is full so that I get a seat if one opens up. | Waitlist entry created with position; promoted automatically to Confirmed on cancellation, in FIFO order. |
| QR Check-in | As an organizer, I want to scan an attendee's QR code so that I can verify entry. | Valid unused QR marks attendance = true; reused QR is rejected with an 'already checked in' message. |

